<item>
            <title>[PLM-1003] Linking Card Match Engine (Pre requisite: Linking via Meditap API)</title>
                <link>https://gooddoctortech.atlassian.net/browse/PLM-1003</link>
                <project id="10125" key="PLM">Platform</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Context:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As per today, Good Doctor have several TPA that supports multiple integrations such as: Admedika, Meditap, Medlinx, Medilink. And Each TPA has its own flow and system including card number that recognized on each system. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Currently, the insurance linking journey requires the member to provide their card/policy number and date of birth. However, the system should not assume that the member understands which TPA manages their insurance coverage.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;So Good Doctor as Provider Service be able to identify the most appropriate TPA based on member provided information and matching it with pattern that spesific into TPA logic under Good Doctor. This ensures faster processing, easier scalability, and lower risk of errors compared to maintaining scattered hardcoded rules.&lt;/p&gt;



&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Definition of Done:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;User be able to link with their respective member code that match with pattern matched logic that stored in Good Doctor&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Admin can insert pattern logic member code with priority and TPA&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Admin can set toggle on Channel Management for Card Match Engine&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;




